WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.280
One over one times two.

2
00:00:02.330 --> 00:00:05.090
Plus one over two times three.

3
00:00:05.140 --> 00:00:07.900
Plus one over three times four.

4
00:00:07.950 --> 00:00:12.550
On it goes, all the way to one
over ninety-nine times one hundred.

5
00:00:12.600 --> 00:00:18.230
A calculator grinds through every term
and lands on a strikingly tidy fraction.

6
00:00:18.280 --> 00:00:20.350
Why is this sum so neat?

7
00:00:20.400 --> 00:00:22.800
Do the terms form a geometric series?

8
00:00:22.850 --> 00:00:25.330
Or is it just a lucky coincidence?

9
00:00:25.380 --> 00:00:28.610
In this mission, you'll
add two fractions into one,

10
00:00:28.660 --> 00:00:30.520
over a single denominator.

11
00:00:30.570 --> 00:00:32.580
Then you'll run that backwards.

12
00:00:32.630 --> 00:00:36.440
Partial fractions split one
fraction into simpler pieces.

13
00:00:36.490 --> 00:00:38.810
You'll find those pieces from an identity,

14
00:00:38.860 --> 00:00:42.190
using values of x that
make each factor zero.

15
00:00:42.240 --> 00:00:46.580
Your mission: work out why this
sum, all the way to ninety-nine,

16
00:00:46.630 --> 00:00:47.730
is so neat.
